d 'CVMTEST': module to perform a k-sample Cramer-von Mises equality-of-distributions test
d
d  cvmtest performs a (optionally weighted) k-sample Cramer-von
d Mises (CVM) permutation test to assess whether k >= 2 samples
d come from the same distribution, as proposed by Kiefer (1959). It
d is the k-sample generalization of the two-sample test (Cramer
d 1928; von Mises 1931).  When k > 2, there is no single pairwise
d comparison to make, so cvmtest instead compares each group's
d empirical CDF to the (weighted) pooled empirical CDF of all
d groups combined. 
d
d KW: equality of distributions
d KW: k-sample
d KW: comparisons
d KW: weighting
d
d Requires: Stata version 11
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260805
d
d Author: Ariel Linden, Linden Consulting Group, LLC
d Support: email alinden@@lindenconsulting.org
d
f cvmtest.ado
f cvmtest.sthlp
